As the author of ctrace, and a reader of netnews for the last couple of
years, I can definitely say that it was not posted to net.sources.  There
were some debugging C preprocessor macros posted.

I gave a talk on ctrace at UNICOM last January (see proceedings) and have
received many requests for it since then.  It is likely to be in the next
release of UNIX, but since System V had just been announced it looked like
it would be some time before the next version was released.  I applied to
have ctrace licensed as a separate product, but when I last checked on it
the request was still sitting in a folder in Western Electric Technology
Licensing in Greensboro, NC.  Keith Testor is the latest of several people
to be keeper of this folder; I don't have an outside phone number for him
but you can try calling Western Electric Software Sales and Marketing
(919) 697-6530.

